Gene Schall. American baseball player (born 1970)
Eugene David Schall (born June 5, 1970) is a retired Major League Baseball first baseman. He played during two seasons at the major league level for the Philadelphia Phillies. He was drafted by the Phillies in the 4th round of the 1991 amateur draft. Schall played his first professional season with their Class A (Short Season) Batavia Clippers in 1991, and his last with their Triple-A Scranton/Wilkes-Barre Red Barons in 2002. Schall played college baseball at Villanova, earning All-Tournament honors after the 1989 Big East Conference baseball tournament. He was named an ABCA All-American in 1991. References. &lt;templatestyles src="Reflist/styles.css" /&gt;
